Entities written with HTML 4.01's names: &infin;, &rarr;, &rArr;, &larr;, &uarr; and &darr;, &rarr; and &larr;, &hellip; and &hellip;, &lowast;, &Aring;, &plusmn;, &ne;, &le; and &ge;, &isin;, &part;, &sdot;, &sect;, &dagger;, &epsilon;, &thetasym;, &lang;x&rang;, &bull; and &clubs;.

With their own names where HTML has them: &alpha;, &vert; and &rarr;.

As themselves: / and _.

With the HTML Standard's names, HTML 4.01 having none: &daleth; and &ctdot;.